    "research": {
      "notes": "**Himax (HIMX), news 2026-09-28 to 2026-10-28**\n\n**1. Guidance**\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal found in the window. The Q3 guidance dates from before it: revenue up 7–11% QoQ, gross margin around 34%, and EPS of 8.0–10.0 cents per diluted ADS — 2026-08-06 — https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/08/06/3339987/0/en/himax-technologies-inc-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results-provides-third-quarter-2026-guidance.html\n- Himax said Q2 revenue, gross margin and EPS all beat its guidance — 2026-08-06 — https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/08/06/3339987/0/en/himax-technologies-inc-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results-provides-third-quarter-2026-guidance.html\n- Himax set the Q3 results call for Nov 5, 2026 at 8:00 AM EST. The announcement came on 2026-10-05, and Q3 results are the next catalyst — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/corporate-news/himax-sets-november-5-results-date-for-himax-technologies-stock/70423317\n- Q3 guidance includes about $11.8M of employee bonus expense, versus about $0.2M in each of the prior three quarters — 2026-08-06 — https://scanx.trade/stock-market-news/companies/himax-technologies-schedules-q3-2026-earnings-call-nov-5/52722472\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- Wall Street Zen cut HIMX from \"buy\" to \"hold\" — 2026-10-24 — https://www.defenseworld.net/2026/10/24/himax-technologies-nasdaqhimx-stock-moved-down-to-hold-by-wall-street-zen.html\n- Danelfin, a quant AI model, set a 3-month target of $12.27 — 2026-10-16 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/nebenwerte/danelfin-puts-a-usd-12-27-target-on-himax-technologies-stock/70348405\n- I found no upgrade, downgrade, initiation or target change from a sell-side broker in the window.\n- Consensus figures conflict:\n  - MarketBeat shows three Holds with an $8.00 average target — 2026-10-24 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/corporate-news/robeco-adds-882-739-shares-himax-technologies-stock-sits-54-88-percent-below-its-high/70406339\n  - Financhill shows a $30.20 consensus target, with two Buys and one Hold — 2026-10-20 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/nebenwerte/financhill-cites-usd-30-20-target-for-himax-technologies-stock/70376990\n  - Investing.com lists Baird at Buy with a $30 target (2026-05-08) and Morgan Stanley at Hold (2026-02-04) — https://www.investing.com/equities/himax-tech-consensus-estimates\n  - Both consensus figures appear to rest on stale broker actions. The $8.00 consensus appears to reflect an older Morgan Stanley target.\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- Nothing material found for Himax: no lawsuits, investigations, fines or Himax-specific export-control actions. The tariff and export-control results I found were general macro items, not Himax-specific.\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- Alibaba chose Himax's WiseEye ultralow-power AI processor for its new Qwen Glasses N1 — 2026-10-14 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/\n- I found no new disclosure of customer concentration, contract losses or contract changes in the window.\n- Automotive was over 50% of Q2 revenue, per the Q2 call on 2026-08-06 (before the window) — https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61838393/himax-techs-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript\n\n**5. Insider activity**\nAll items are RSU vestings. I found no open-market buys or sells, no 10b5-1 sales and no clustered selling.\n- CEO Jordan Wu: 6,806 RSUs vested, giving 13,612 shares acquired. He held 540,253 shares afterward — 2026-09-30 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/HIMX/form-4-himax-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-1311c4a04f1d.html\n- CFO Pan Ming-Feng: acquired 3,916 shares on RSU vesting and held 129,372 shares afterward — 2026-09-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001342338/000117184326006301/ownership.xml\n- Wu was also granted 4,797 RSUs on 2026-09-24, just before the window opened — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/HIMX/form-4-himax-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-8fd926f2382d.html\n\n**6. Product and competitive news**\n- The Alibaba Qwen Glasses N1 design win (see section 4) is the main product item in the window — 2026-10-14 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/\n- Himax launched the HX83196/HX83197 eDP TDDI chips for automotive displays on 2026-09-08, before the window. It also showed automotive display and 3D sensing at the SID symposium on Sept 15–16 — https://briefglance.com/companies/himax-technologies-inc\n- On co-packaged optics (CPO), management said on 2026-08-06 that Gen 1 and Gen 2 products began engineering production ramps in Q3, with more meaningful volume from 2027 — https://www.quiverquant.com/news/Himax+Technologies+Reports+Q2+2026+Results+Above+Guidance;+Raises+Q3+Outlook+on+Automotive+and+Emerging+Growth+Momentum\n- On the Q2 call, the CEO said competitors use traditional molded-glass optics, whereas Himax uses wafer-level optics — 2026-08-06 — https://gloom.sh/stocks/himx/transcripts/q2-2026\n- Industry-wide foundry, packaging and testing capacity constraints are raising Himax's costs and lead times — 2026-08-06 — https://www.quiverquant.com/news/Himax+Technologies+Reports+Q2+2026+Results+Above+Guidance;+Raises+Q3+Outlook+on+Automotive+and+Emerging+Growth+Momentum\n\n**Price context:** HIMX fell 17.3% over 2026-09-25 to 2026-10-27 and closed at $11.94 on 2026-10-27 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/",
